# Next.js 15 App Router rules

## Ground rules

- Server Components by default. Add "use client" only where interactivity requires it, at the lowest leaf possible.
- Data fetching lives in Server Components or Route Handlers. No client-side fetch for initial page data.
- Never import server-only modules (db, env secrets, fs) into client components. If it needs a secret, it runs on the server.
- Mutations go through Server Actions with input validation (zod) at the boundary. Revalidate affected paths explicitly.

## Code style

- TypeScript strict. No `any` without a comment explaining why.
- File conventions: page.tsx, layout.tsx, loading.tsx, error.tsx, route.ts. Colocate only what one route uses; shared code goes in /lib or /components.
- Images via next/image, fonts via next/font. No raw <img> tags.
- Metadata via the metadata export, never hardcoded <head> tags.

## Definition of done

- [ ] `npm run build` passes with no warnings
- [ ] `npm test` passes; new behavior has a failing-then-passing test
- [ ] No new client components without a stated reason in the PR
- [ ] Loading and error states exist for every new route
